# src/tychoc.c:8336 -- every branch dies, so the value if/match has no tail to
# bind and the local would be declared void.
# No pinned expectation: scored against ./tychoc1, which has no divergence
# analysis -- `_tail_type` reads `die(...)` as void, so it refuses this as
# `cannot bind a void value`, the same message it gives value_ctrl_void_branch.ty.
# Telling the two apart is a real change, not a wording port.
fn main():
    x := if true:
        die("a")
    else:
        die("b")
    println(str(x))
